course: dictionary
lesson: 6224
title: Mix: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mix is a small word with several meanings, so read the words around it to find the one you need. «Never mix old and new batteries in the same toy.» Here mix means put things together so they become one. The warning tells you not to combine them.
explain: «Being open about money stops mix-ups in families.» A mix-up is a confusion, when two things get muddled. Here mix means muddle, and the word up joins it. The clue is in the phrase, not only in the single word.
explain: «Accents grow from the people who settle a place, and their mix became the Australian accent.» Here mix is a noun, a blend of many different groups. Try your meaning in the sentence: their blend became the accent. It still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: «Mix» can be a verb (to mix, mixes, mixed, mixing) or a noun (a mix).
fact: «Mix» means to put different things together so they become one.
fact: «A mix» is what you get when you combine things, or a packet ready to use, such as cake mix.
fact: «Mix with people» means to meet and talk with them.
fact: «Mix up» means to confuse two things. Trail mix and mix and match are useful phrases too.
exercise: «Never mix old and new batteries in the same toy.» What does mix mean here? | Cook a cake | Meet and talk with | Confuse, get muddled | *Put together so they become one
exercise: Ella says, «Please don't mix up my bag with yours.» What does mix up mean? | Count them slowly | Pack them very neatly | *Confuse two things | Tip them out on the floor
exercise: «Accents grow from the people who settle a place, and their mix became the Australian accent.» What kind of word is mix in this sentence? | *A noun: a blend of different groups | A verb meaning to dig | An adjective meaning wet | A name for a place
test: Which phrase means «to meet and talk with people»? | Mix and match | *Mix with people | Mix up | Trail mix
test: «Water with impurities, like tap water, can conduct electricity.» In «tiny bits of other things mixed in it», what does mixed mean? | Frozen solid | *Put in with the water, so they are part of it | Poured out slowly | Washed away from the water
exam: In «Grandma bought a cake mix», what is mix? | A verb: to stir or combine | *A noun: a packet ready to use | An adjective: sticky | A command to stop
